From c792662ac80d7e7c8b84c090a8299b04df0c75d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lbgos <285507185+lbgos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:58:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/46] rift_s: require a full radio response header before
 consuming it

The completion path below asserts ret > 3, but a 2-3 byte read fell
through and was consumed with an uninitialised busy flag. Bail on
short reads to match.

(cherry picked from commit 058bd2f4b6e637ff2f5c05900d545b72e10c0dd4)
---
 src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_radio.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_radio.c b/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_radio.c
index b4cfb81..781a32a 100644
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_radio.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_radio.c
@@ -79,8 +79,10 @@ rift_s_radio_update(rift_s_radio_state *state, struct os_hid_device *hid)
 		 * has incremented */
 		int ret = get_radio_response_report(hid, &radio_response);
 
-		if (ret < 2) {
-			break; /* HID read failed - bail */
+		/* The busy flag and seqnum occupy the first three bytes; a shorter
+		 * read carries no usable fields (busy_flag would be uninitialised stack). */
+		if (ret < 4) {
+			break; /* HID read failed or short - bail */
 		}
 
 		if (radio_response.busy_flag != 0x00 || radio_response.seqnum == state->last_radio_seqnum) {
-- 
